</node>
<node id="Chương Trình Đào Tạo Thạc Sĩ (list)">
  <data key="d0">Chương Trình Đào Tạo Thạc Sĩ (list)</data>
  <data key="d1">list</data>
  <data key="d2">This list details master's program requirements, including curriculum structure, faculty roles, assessment methods, and financial information. It supports student understanding of academic expectations and aligns with institutional regulations (ĐHQG-HCM) and student rights (ĐVCM, ĐVQL) outlined in surrounding content. Key elements ensure transparency in program delivery and administrative procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5815d3f799412487de4e05251fac67e</data>
  <data key="d4">cam_nang_sau_dai_hoc_2025_0.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1779107566</data>
</node>
<node id="Master's Program Structure and Credit Requirements (page_number)">
  <data key="d0">Master's Program Structure and Credit Requirements (page_number)</data>
  <data key="d1">page_number</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 5 outlines the three-part structure of the Master's program, requiring a minimum of 60 credits. It details components: general knowledge, specialized studies, and research/thesis. This section defines academic requirements and aligns with training objectives, ensuring alignment with regulatory frameworks and program outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d32e42330071c29105d35ae74aab510</data>
  <data key="d4">cam_nang_sau_dai_hoc_2025_0.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1779107566</data>
</node>
<node id="Section 6 - Program Structure (page_number)">
  <data key="d0">Section 6 - Program Structure (page_number)</data>
  <data key="d1">page_number</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 6 outlines the structural framework of master's programs, detailing credit distribution (60 TC minimum), three core components (general knowledge, specialized courses, thesis/research), and program-specific requirements. It distinguishes between research (53 TC thesis with Q2 journal publications) and applied programs (12 TC thesis), emphasizing academic rigor and professional relevance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6bc260d86ccdc6751f55c8fe280e952</data>
  <data key="d4">cam_nang_sau_dai_hoc_2025_0.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1779107566</data>
</node>
<node id="Page 6 - Application Requirements for Training Methods (page_number)">
  <data key="d0">Page 6 - Application Requirements for Training Methods (page_number)</data>
  <data key="d1">page_number</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 6 serves as a navigational marker preceding administrative requirements for master's program enrollment. It connects to sections detailing eligibility criteria, publication mandates, and documentation processes for distinct training methods (research method 1, research method 2, and application programs). This page reinforces the document's focus on structured academic governance and compliance with institutional standards for postgraduate education.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c89eb4f14009f087896aeb466b6a978</data>
  <data key="d4">cam_nang_sau_dai_hoc_2025_0.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1779107566</data>
</node>
