</node>
<node id="Scholarship Criteria for Master's Program: Type 1 and Type 2 (table)">
  <data key="d0">Scholarship Criteria for Master's Program: Type 1 and Type 2 (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">This table details the minimum criteria and scholarship amounts for Type 1 and Type 2 scholarships under the Master's program. Type 1 requires high-impact publications (SCI/SCIE, NAFOSTED, Scopus-Q1, CORE A*), offering 100% support, while Type 2 awards 50% for UIT Honors Challenge special recognition. It reflects the document's focus on merit-based, transparent scholarship allocation, aligning with the principles of fairness and academic excellence outlined in the surrounding regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74d67409d43ac7950af086d744fcff51</data>
  <data key="d4">cam_nang_sau_dai_hoc_2025_0.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1779118997</data>
</node>
